  "music": "w2-sizzle-street",
  "authorNotes": "Solo, two checkpoints, three segments — the escalation stacks the belt and the pan on the same obstacle instead of visiting them one at a time. Grab relic-bread right at spawn (320,850). Seg 1 is a plain swing (swing-escalate-a, 260px), familiar ground. Seg 2 is the escalate: belt-hazard (1500,860 to 2450,860, speed 95, 950px, no plank) carries you the whole way, but pan-belt (1850,860, 1.2s grace) sits embedded in the belt's own surface partway along — the belt keeps pulling you forward automatically, so dawdling on the hot patch is a choice, not a trap, but a cautious player can instead grab rope-bypass (anchor 1950,520, directly above the pan) and swing clear of the belt entirely rather than riding through the hot stretch. relic-veggie waits on the far counter (2650,790), past the belt, before a short grease patch (2800-3020) that slicks the final approach. Seg 3 is a plain swing (swing-escalate-final, 300px) to the goal counter, where plate-vegan-sandwich (3550,770) takes both ingredients for the recipe objective. Assist beams span all three true gaps at the usual Clock cost — the seg-2 beam bridges the belt+pan combo directly, matching rope-bypass as a second way to skip it."
